KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ outer handler reached after rethrow: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ outer rethrow re-propagates the outer exception E\(1\): SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
KNOWNBUG: [except.throw]/8 -- a rethrow in an outer handler that encloses a
completed inner try/catch re-propagates the inner exception instead of the outer
one.  remove_cpp_exceptions keeps the exception being handled in a single pair of
"current exception" globals rather than a stack, so the inner handler clobbers
the outer exception (assertion 2 currently FAILS, VERIFICATION FAILED).  Flip to
CORE once the current-exception state is a stack across nested handlers.
